iptive, not independent data replications.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Guided budget-averaged disruption exceeds each comparator on every panel. At the smallest NBA 2014 budget, guidance ties the small-margin control; the other plotted seed-averaged cells favor guidance. This does not imply universally positive paired uncertainty.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"All Arena paired intervals are strictly positive; all degree-stratified NBA intervals include zero. NBA 2012 small-margin comparisons are positive for all seeds; NBA 2011 small-margin and NBA 2012 uniform each have one wholly positive interval. NBA 2013\\u20132015 intervals all include zero.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Arena finite-shift discrepancy spans 0.2235\\u20130.3350; NBA spans about 0.00036\\u20130.02274. This is a normalized coefficient-shift diagnostic, not rank error, superiority, or an accuracy threshold.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\",\n        \"final.metric.influence_error\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"implementation_evidence\": [\n        \"source_evidence/task_contract.json:method.audits\"\n      ],\n      \"support_scope\": \"Registered final evidence identifies the evaluated condition; readable documentation, not hashes or metric values, supports implementation specifics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Recorded CPU evaluation durations span approximately 29.6\\u201330.5 seconds per seed evaluation, not method-only timings or speedup measurements.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/0/duration_seconds\",\n        \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/1/duration_seconds\",\n        \"paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes/2/duration_seconds\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The fixed estimator uses sum logistic loss with unit quadratic ridge, centered participant scores, fractional uneditable ties, and a regularized optional NBA home effect. Nominal fractions .001, .005, .01 use all rows and floor-rounded nested binary flips.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"implementation_evidence\": [\n        \"source_evidence/flip_search.py:22-44\",\n        \"source_evidence/flip_search.py:61-172\",\n        \"source_evidence/task_contract.json:method.scientific_workload\"\n      ],\n      \"support_scope\": \"Registered final evidence identifies the evaluated condition; readable documentation, not hashes or metric values, supports implementation specifics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Influence screening uses genuine Hessian derivatives, a frozen top-min(10,p) adjacent contrast, width-two exact-refitted path selection, and up to six nearby contrast proposals. The lexicographic internal objective leads with summed displacement, not the reported inversion fraction.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"implementation_evidence\": [\n        \"source_evidence/flip_search.py:194-266\",\n        \"source_evidence/flip_search.py:510-549\"\n      ],\n      \"support_scope\": \"Registered final evidence identifies the evaluated condition; readable documentation, not hashes or metric values, supports implementation specifics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The available source implements strict complete-path swaps/replacements with sorted original-row prefix caching and incumbent fallback. It uses up to 24 sampled positions, additional refit caps 72 or 24 by dimension, a two-second optional deadline, and 128 proposals; no execution trace establishes accepted exchange counts or isolated exchange benefit.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"implementation_evidence\": [\n        \"source_evidence/flip_search.py:309-475\"\n      ],\n      \"support_scope\": \"Registered final evidence identifies the evaluated condition; readable documentation, not hashes or metric values, supports implementation specifics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The available solver uses damped Newton/Cholesky with at most 50 Newton steps, L-BFGS fallback and final stationarity rejection at gradient infinity norm above 1e-6; these are code settings, not measured operation counts.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": [],\n      \"implementation_evidence\": [\n        \"source_evidence/flip_search.py:119-172\"\n      ],\n      \"support_scope\": \"Registered final evidence identifies the evaluated condition; readable documentation, not hashes or metric values, supports implementation specifics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Uniform, approximate degree-quartile-stratified and small-margin controls share integer budgets. The three-budget average, equal seeds, half Arena/half equal-season NBA weighting and thirty-resample fixed-plan grouped bootstrap define the reporting protocol.\",\n   