ied fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/final/nba-2015.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"a114460aa6d904ea9763dbc375061873e4e9ab88ca1df78ea7be727220030535\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/search/arena.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"2ceec92b9becbccd637b9aba0a642e840bb4b3990c2597ec6b98d428c65c47fd\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/search/manifest.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"ca19fcd04db8428c2189c7409bfc0843ed03cf5c6e865d7efb833d69a5e53920\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/search/nba-2006.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"bdc30cc36443be87be9e04bcea78394d0bed87ecdccf75b8d99dd2293343e00e\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/search/nba-2007.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"eb27089862a9f7e4bd51a356237b48256ab900a45123e2d568c06007873227d2\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/search/nba-2008.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"da24ea302d9eedc090da7c2247ded80b0dcbe83ff72705b75cae94b6e2451f15\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"reproducible_preparation\",\n        \"path\": \"prepare_data.py\",\n        \"sha256\": \"e2958fe33c11c41519f2e2c336c3767df87cb0c2c0313b8dd26c705cd5671838\",\n        \"source\": \"Task-authored deterministic raw-source checksum, normalized document/example union-find split and reciprocal-game audit.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"pinned_direct_dependencies\",\n        \"path\": \"requirements.txt\",\n        \"sha256\": \"393d9162235ee3676b301ed71a254a322c488be9c7ac3c4928ec5e23cee085f1\",\n        \"source\": \"Exact identities/versions verified against https://pypi.org/pypi/numpy/2.2.6/json, https://pypi.org/pypi/scipy/1.15.3/json and https://pypi.org/pypi/matplotlib/3.10.3/json.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"harness_compatibility\",\n        \"path\": \"capture.py\",\n        \"sha256\": \"9ccd8975f287cca981934eb4fdb5ff223a1c26d15056396da67338fd77d556c6\",\n        \"source\": \"Task-authored safe OutputCapture compatibility artifact.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_evaluator\",\n        \"path\": \"evaluate.py\",\n        \"sha256\": \"321cf0812a35e81d232de440a1845b5e93c2a4eacb9d2c690d083d1f1937a062\",\n        \"source\": \"Task-authored self-contained independent regularized Newton refits and bounded evaluator-owned controls.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_evaluator\",\n        \"path\": \"evaluate_final.py\",\n        \"sha256\": \"39ba2cda512794e4cb13737549cc52e87aa77b771315eb73facd215d973f2833\",\n        \"source\": \"Task-authored self-contained sealed evaluator. No search imports or search resource reads.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"compute\": {\n    \"search\": {\n      \"accelerator\": \"cpu\",\n      \"accelerator_model\": \"none\",\n      \"gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"evaluator_gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"candidate_gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"cpu_cores\": 4,\n      \"memory_gb\": 8,\n      \"precision\": \"float64\",\n      \"wall_clock_seconds\": 3600,\n      \"max_candidate_rpc_calls\": 444\n    },\n    \"final\": {\n      \"accelerator\": \"cpu\",\n      \"accelerator_model\": \"none\",\n      \"gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"evaluator_gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"candidate_gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"cpu_cores\": 4,\n      \"memory_gb\": 8,\n      \"precision\": \"float64\",\n      \"wall_clock_seconds\": 14400,\n      \"max_candidate_rpc_calls\": 666\n    }\n  },\n  \"protocol\": {\n    \"search_seeds\": [\n      101,\n      211,\n      307\n    ],\n    \"final_seeds\": [\n      401,\n      503,\n      607\n    ],\n    \"search_reset_sequence\": [\n      101,\n      101,\n      101,\n      101,\n      211,\n      211,\n      211,\n      211,\n      307,\n      307,\n      307,\n      307\n    ],\n    \"search_smoke_reset_sequence\": [\n      101,\n      101,\n      101,\n      101\n    ],\n    \"final_reset_sequence\": [\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      503,\n      503,\n      503,\n      503,\n      503,\n      503,\n      607,\n      607,\n      607,\n      607,\n      607,\n      607\n    ],\n    \"final_smoke_reset_sequence\": [\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401\n    ],\n    \"baselines\": [\n      \"unmodified_copy\",\n      \"uniform_random_flips\",\n      \"degree_sum_quartile_matched_flips\",\n      \"close_margin_heuristic\",\n      \"synthetic_constant_zero\",\n      \"permuted_influence_priorities\",\n      \"reset_no_data\"\n    ],\n    \"promotion_rule\": \"Development-only integrity-eligible ranking by descending combined_score, ties earlier submission then digest. At most three complete search submissions, one frozen sealed final invocation; harness exclusively owns promotion/freezing/publication. No comparative threshold, final-feedback tuning, replay or retries.\",\n    \"search_proxies\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"smaller_content_panel\",\n        \"preserves\": \"Real crowdsourced preferences, normalized document groups, genuine binary flips and independent fixed-L2 BT refits, all four controls and both evaluation designs.\",\n        \"omits\": \"Remaining sealed Arena groups and later NBA seasons; cannot establish temporal generalization or publication-quality evidence alone.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"lighter_uncertainty\",\n        \"preserves\": \"Fixed paired group bootstrap, fixed weights, matched edit budgets and all planned cases/seeds.\",\n        \"omits\": \"Final uses 8 instead of4 random streams,30 instead of10 resamples and five instead of three sports seasons.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"feedback\": {\n    \"search_visible\": [\n      \"Search scalar metrics and correctness, validated search-only solution evidence; fixed bounded failure categories. Raw worker stderr is repair-only under exact drafting/qualification flags.\",\n      \"Observed search episode comparison endpoints/outcomes and public workload/model settings through documented RPC only.\"\n    ],\n    \"final_sealed\": [\n      \"Final resource panels, manifests, seed constants, reference fits, metrics, correctness, controls and solution evidence are sealed until freeze and never optimization feedback.\",\n      \"During final execution candidate receives only observed final comparisons and plane-independent workload/model inputs, never held-out answers, scores or baseline outputs.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"publication\": {\n    \"search_is_proxy\": true,\n    \"requires_final_evaluation\": true,\n    \"required_evidence\": [\n      \"A complete research paper, PDF and LaTeX source in the latest officially released NeurIPS main-conference template available when preparing the submission; document the chosen edition and comply with its actual page limit and required checklist. Include abstract, introduction, genuinely read related work, intervention/model methods, real-data experiments, uncertainty, discussion, limitations and references. Obtain and record official template provenance downstream; no template or completed paper is claimed to exist at design time.\",\n      \"Real results on both the crowdsourced Arena panel and season-specific NBA panels, including every declared case/seed/budget, baseline stream and control, with normalized edit-cost definitions, why two different designs are comparable, graph/participant coverage and clear limits from unequal data volumes, temporal change, ties, home advantage, regularization and non-causal cross-design comparisons. Report null and adverse results equally. Do not imply that these datasets represent all leaderboards or identify malicious behavior.\",\n      \"Verified pinned-source checksums and licenses, raw-data acquisition instructions, evaluator-owned source IDs and row provenance, normalization specification, complete raw-document/example SHA-256 manifests and demonstrated search/final content disjointness before feature extraction. Document reciprocal NBA rows, excluded invalid records, connectedness and split-induced selection. Raw data stays in working data storage, not the code repository or paper submission; do not redistribute private split material or unnecessary text. Source checksums quoted in task.md are expected values, not design-time verification evidence.\",\n      \"Reproducible genuine candidate influence computation and trusted independent Bradley-Terry reference/refit code; fixed estimator and edit-feasibility policy; finite-difference and actual-refit audits; matched-budget baseline/control results including rejected vacuous permutations and reset-state tests. Pairwise comparative claims require the corresponding baseline contrasts and uncertainty. Missing or failed evidence retains finite worst-case values, full fixed weights and explicit failure status. No comparison advantage, stability conclusion or causal alignment result may be inferred from an incomplete or vacuous control.\",\n      \"Separate reports of scientific validity, search eligibility and final claim assessment, including exact search and final correct predicates, score hierarchy and weights, predeclared tie policy, all three-or-fewer search submissions and failures, frozen candidate digest/configuration, final unsealing chronology and the single final invocation. Novelty and publication standards are not post hoc search thresholds. State which narrower claims remain justified if comparisons are inconclusive.\",\n      \"Downstream contract preflight with canonical task digest, actual source/dependency provenance and synchronized artifact hashes; exact production/smoke reset arrays matching case/seed cardinality and order globally across clients/restarts; no unplanned resets or replays; actual largest production request/response JSON serialization sizes including UTF-8, base64, metadata, envelope and framing; bounded candidate-RAM chunk sessions; and fully counted max_candidate_rpc_calls covering resets, stale-token checks, chunks, failures and retries. No shared filesystem or path-based RPC. This design specifies required evidence; it does not claim preflight has already passed.\",\n      \"Offline smoke validation for both planes through unchanged loader/import/device/mount/broker/update/metric paths with reduced work, empty HOME and the exact smoke transcripts. Keep smoke validation distinct from successful full production completion. Provide harness allocation/isolation evidence, all-thread CPU policy, actual monotonic times and cleanup/cancellation logs. Clearly distinguish enforced wall/RPC/resource ceilings from advisory candidate-internal iteration counts; do not present reported iteration counters as a trusted hard operation cap.\",\n      \"All paper numbers, plots and tables must come from actual recorded task runs with scripts mapping each output to inputs, seeds, configuration and trusted metrics. Provide code, standard requirements.txt versions, offline wheel/platform instructions, data-fetch commands, reproduction commands and measured or honestly labeled estimated runtimes. Log failures, abandoned approaches, unfinished analyses and LLM assistance. Never fabricate checkpoints, measurements, successful launches, read literature or completed validation.\",\n      \"Respect the canonical independence restriction: never identify, guess, search for, access or use the prohibited prior paper or any related mirror, abstract, discussion, reproduction or code. Use only explicitly allowed starter readings and unrelated permitted sources, avoid broad searches likely to encounter forbidden material, and immediately stop and record any accidental encounter with location and amount read. Network is restricted to listed data acquisition, permissible literature and dependency installation; no paid APIs. Finish research, experiments, writing and reproduction within the one-week task budget.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
